)","-                    <if(item.hasNext)>,<endif>","-                }>","-            ;","-            \"\"\";","-","     private static final String FIND_BY_TRACE_IDS = \"\"\"","             SELECT DISTINCT project_id, trace_id, id_week","             FROM span_weeks","             WHERE workspace_id = :workspace_id","             AND trace_id IN :trace_ids","-            AND is_deleted = 0","             SETTINGS log_comment = '<log_comment>'","             \"\"\";"," ","+    /**","+     * Registers the week of every span in one chunk's id range. The range only selects which spans are read, pruning","+     * granules through the {@code idx_spans_id} minmax index; each span's week comes from its id, with the","+     * {@code spans_local_v2} partition expression rather than {@code id_at}, which the legacy {@code spans} declares as","+     * a 32-bit {@code DateTime} that wraps far-future ids.","+     * <p>","+     * Threads are capped so the backfill stays a small share of the server; memory is left to the profile's","+     * {@code max_bytes_ratio_before_external_group_by} spill. {@code optimize_aggregation_in_order = 0} is the server","+     * default, kept explicit because in-order aggregation over the sort key measured ~200x slower for this","+     * {@code GROUP BY}, so a profile that enabled it would stall the backfill.","+     */","+    private static final String BACKFILL = \"\"\"","+            INSERT INTO span_weeks (workspace_id, project_id, trace_id, id_week)","+            SELECT workspace_id, project_id, trace_id,","+                toUInt32(toYYYYMMDD(toDate32(toDateTime64(UUIDv7ToDateTime(toUUID(id)), 0, 'UTC'))","+                    - toIntervalDay(toDayOfWeek(toDateTime64(UUIDv7ToDateTime(toUUID(id)), 0, 'UTC'), 1)))) AS week","+            FROM spans","+            WHERE true","+            <if(from_id)>AND id >= :from_id<endif>","+            <if(to_id)>AND id \\\\< :to_id<endif>","+            GROUP BY workspace_id, project_id, trace_id, wee